 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nFor more information see the section on the Budget Billing Plan component.\n\nSecurity Deposits\n\nUse\n\nYou can request a security deposit in move-in processing, or, provided certain conditions have been met, adopt the security\ndeposit of an existing contract.\n\nRe-Request Security Deposit\nCustomizing Settings\n\nIn Customizing under |)}Move-In/Out Move-In 's Define Move-In Control Parameters on Contract Level \u201cyou can configure the\n\nsystem so that security deposits are requested through move-in processing.You can request a cash security deposit, or arrange a\nnon-cash security deposit with the customer.\n\ne Acash security deposit is created for each contract. In doing this, this system posts a request document for a cash security\ndeposit in FI-CA.\n\ne Anon-cash security deposit is created for all the contracts involved in the move-in, for which a non-cash deposit is to be\n\ncreated.\nEntry Options on the Move-In Screen\n\nOn the move-in screen, on the tabstrip Contract Data , enter a reason for requesting the security deposit and the amount\nrequested. Now, when you save the move-in document, the system automatically creates a security deposit. If you specified a\nreason for exempting the customer from a security deposit then one is not created. You can allocate a default value to the security\n\ndeposit reason and amount using enhancement EC500001 (determine security deposit reason and amount).\n\nFor more information see the section on Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable (FI-CA) including Security Deposits .\n\nAdopt Existing Security Deposits (Transfer)\n\nIn Customizing under Define Move-In Control Parameters on Contract Level , you can, using the Security deposits field,\nconfigure the system to transfer the security deposits of existing contracts to newly created contracts. This is done by means of\nTransfer Contracts. You can use this procedure if, for example, a business partner moves to a new premise in the supply territory,\nterminates his/her existing contracts for this reason and wishes the security deposits paid on these contracts to be adopted for\nthe new contracts. You can transfer deposits in this way if the following transfer conditions have been met:\n\ne You have entered a move-in/out in the system.\n\ne You have selected the contracts so that both the move-in and move-out documents both contain one contract for each\ndivision, and each have the same number of contracts.\n\ne In Customizing, under Define Move-In Control Parameters on Contract Level , you have defined whether the security\ndeposits of a contract can be automatically transferred.\n\ne Both the transfer contract and the new contract have been allocated to the same company code.\n",
